<title>JAPAN: Bangchak awards Oman in April cargo tender-sources.</title>
<headline>Bangchak awards Oman in April cargo tender-sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangchak Petroleum Plc's refinery purchased one million barrels of Oman cargoes for April lifting in its buying tender, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said a Japanese trading company had been awarded a contract to sell 500,000 barrels of Oman at a discount of three cents to the official selling price. Some traders added that the award had been made under attractive credit terms that made the deal actually closer to MPM minus four cents.</p>
<p>A European major was rumoured to have sold the same volume at MPM flat, sources said.</p>
</text>
